Goal: code a newcomer understands on first read — not the fewest lines.

## The loop

1. Checks are green; take only the phase's diff ([01]({{ref_01}})).
2. Understand callers, side effects, error paths and tests ([02]({{ref_02}})).
3. Name the smell from the catalog; skip code that is already clear ([03]({{ref_03}})).
4. One small simplification → rerun formatter/analyzer and affected tests.
5. Stop at the stop criteria ([04]({{ref_04}})).
6. Report one line ([05]({{ref_05}})).

